(7297936, 1137802, 50864, '<td valign="top">Dang, I went by this too fast. Luckily Don didn''t. Great use of "break the rules". Congratulations on the ph blue.</td>', 'Dang, I went by this too fast. Luckily Don didn''t. Great use of "break the rules". Congratulations on the ph blue.', '2015-01-02 11:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7297945, 1137677, 119012, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by damjanev:</b></div><hr/><i> Even with the description and the original shot this looks alike a legit edit in "Advanced". </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>since when are we allowed to remove image area in advanced editing? maybe the shadow would be considered legal since it was shadow, but i''ve seen dq''s for burning down an area so it was obscured even if it was edge of the image.<br/> <br/>i figured removing visible features would be a no-no.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-01-02 14:30:40.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by damjanev: Even with the description and the original shot this looks alike a legit edit in "Advanced".   since when are we allowed to remove image area in advanced editing? maybe the shadow would be considered legal since it was shadow, but i''ve seen dq''s for burning down an area so it was obscured even if it was edge of the image. i figured removing visible features would be a no-no.', '2015-01-02 12:06:24.000000', '2015-01-02 14:30:40.000000', 0),
